/**
@mainpage ORCA code reference

[Back to the ORCA documentation](../docs/radar/code-reference/)

This is the reference for the code in [uhd_radar](https://github.com/HI-SNR-Lab/uhd_radar),
the repository behind the Open Radar Code Architecture (ORCA). Doxygen builds it from the code
and from the comments in the code, so it describes the code exactly as it was at the commit
shown at the top of this page.

## Where to start

| To understand... | Look at |
| --- | --- |
| how a whole run is put together | run.py and the run.RadarProcessRunner class |
| how the chirp is generated before a run | generate_chirp.py |
| the program that talks to the radio | main.cpp, with the Sdr and Chirp classes |
| how recorded data is loaded and processed | processing.py and processing_dask.py |
| the unit tests | the files under tests/ |

Use **Classes** for the C++ classes, **Namespaces** for the Python modules and **Files** to browse
by folder. Every function page links to its source code.

## Why some functions have no description

Doxygen only shows comments written in its own format. The format the project uses is described under
"Doxygen Requirements" in STYLEGUIDE.md. The page "Documentation coverage" on the ORCA documentation
site lists the functions that still need a comment.
*/
